{"id": "swebq0060", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1876622498, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "aa7a8a6f2040793a4fe8dabcb6d10f2520887b0e0988d37809c3a27ef31575d8", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "what team did adrian peterson play for in college?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0060.wav", "input_sha256": "ad75d441d980e9c8dd0b942773c1f223c1b523905888ec76eeff70ac5a21ebc0", "input_samples": 55710, "input_s": 3.482, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.5027, "act": 0.9998, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Adrian Peterson played college football for the Oklahoma Sooners at the University of Oklahoma.", "expert_answer": "Adrian Peterson played college football for the **Oklahoma Sooners** at the **University of Oklahoma**.", "transcript": "What team did Adrian Peterson play for in college?\n", "asr_s": 0.53, "expert_s": 1.94, "expert_input_samples": 55710, "expert_input_s": 3.482, "expert_input_sha256": "ad75d441d980e9c8dd0b942773c1f223c1b523905888ec76eeff70ac5a21ebc0", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 1.679, "relay_synth_ms": 3209, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0060_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "db14c35360b708b8db285f407cbe9f6961afd357a18b7aaf9e6f2e83a48754b9", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 6.56}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0060_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "8722104b7837752b8d4b9916ad5bcae94021b0419cce9d214ec69f70855ffa23", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.36}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.062, 1.112, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.064, 2.115, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.064, 3.114, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 3.482, 3.545, 3.72, 0, 0, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 3.482, "last_real_feed_done": 3.545, "onset": 3.72, "gate_read_done": 3.72, "fire": 3.72, "candidate_first_pcm": null, "stall_note": 3.721, "stall_first_pcm": 4.509, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 4.509, "expert_req": 3.72, "expert_resp": 6.188, "relay_synth_start": 6.188, "relay_first_pcm": 6.901, "relay_synth_end": 9.398, "first_any_pcm": 4.509, "first_answer_pcm": 6.901, "session_end": 9.534}, "ttfa_answer_s": 3.419, "ttfa_any_s": 1.027}
{"id": "swebq0072", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2563747023, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "aa7a8a6f2040793a4fe8dabcb6d10f2520887b0e0988d37809c3a27ef31575d8", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "what are the major trading partners of germany?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0072.wav", "input_sha256": "5994e45b94578c6c0c60f39e23e34b0315071d3e94dc24530bf193fcecab0e65", "input_samples": 46793, "input_s": 2.925, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.5841, "act": 0.9973, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Germany’s major trading partners are China, the United States, and the Netherlands. Germany’s trade is heavily tied to the EU single market, while China and the U.S. are its most important non-European partners.", "expert_answer": "Germany’s major trading partners are **China, the United States, and the Netherlands**. In the latest annual figures cited by Germany’s Federal Statistical Office, **China was Germany’s largest trading partner in 2025**, with total goods trade of about **€251.8 billion**, followed by the **United States** at about **€240.5 billion**; the **Netherlands** was third. ([destatis.de](https://www.destatis.de/EN/Press/2026/02/PE26_056_51.html?utm_source=openai))\n\nOther important partners typically include **France, Poland, Italy, Austria, Switzerland, Belgium, the Czech Republic, and the United Kingdom**, especially within Europe. Germany’s trade is heavily tied to the **EU single market**, while **China and the U.S.** are its most important non-European partners.", "transcript": "What are the major trading partners of Germany?\n", "asr_s": 0.61, "expert_s": 14.83, "expert_input_samples": 46793, "expert_input_s": 2.925, "expert_input_sha256": "5994e45b94578c6c0c60f39e23e34b0315071d3e94dc24530bf193fcecab0e65", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 14.75, "relay_synth_ms": 7075, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0072_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "ff85bc41f2f1ad17c018b9d412b8ec9d2b476aa407c112325fec48bc75f03281", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 14.56}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0072_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "68efdc341bb8fc94c7aed0625caeb02cc1e1ea57fe85ac2baddc9df743e0d90a", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0072_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "fc77a5e3e26322708d10cc025af25117224e03565a4a37aed1fe4141af88fb85", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.062, 1.112, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.064, 2.115, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.925, 2.988, 3.04, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.925, 3.989, 4.453, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.925, "last_real_feed_done": 2.988, "onset": 4.453, "gate_read_done": 4.453, "fire": 4.453, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.453, "stall_note": 4.454, "stall_first_pcm": 5.15, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.15, "expert_req": 4.454, "expert_resp": 19.899, "relay_synth_start": 19.9, "relay_first_pcm": 20.623, "relay_synth_end": 26.975, "first_any_pcm": 4.453, "first_answer_pcm": 20.623, "session_end": 27.115}, "ttfa_answer_s": 17.698, "ttfa_any_s": 1.528}
{"id": "swebq0080", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 4049195308, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "aa7a8a6f2040793a4fe8dabcb6d10f2520887b0e0988d37809c3a27ef31575d8", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "what are republicans views on health care?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0080.wav", "input_sha256": "d57fe5eb396272d1174f540ae6760d1c15e8d49360db9415a0a7d676d89ac24a", "input_samples": 38620, "input_s": 2.414, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.6289, "act": 0.9979, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Republicans generally favor a more market-based health care system with less federal control. In short: Republicans usually argue that health care should be private-sector driven, less regulated, more transparent, and less dependent on federal programs, while still preserving programs like Medicare for eligible seniors. (presidency.ucsb.edu)", "expert_answer": "Republicans generally favor a **more market-based health care system** with less federal control. Common Republican views include:\n\n- **Lower costs through competition and price transparency** among hospitals, insurers, and drug companies.\n- **More consumer choice**, including wider use of private insurance, health savings accounts, and flexible insurance plans.\n- **Opposition to single-payer or “Medicare for All”** style government-run health care.\n- **Skepticism of the Affordable Care Act / Obamacare**, though recent GOP platforms have emphasized lowering costs more than full repeal.\n- **Protecting Medicare for seniors**, with the 2024 GOP platform saying Republicans would protect Medicare and Social Security.\n- **Medicaid reform**, often favoring work requirements, state flexibility, or limits on federal spending rather than broad expansion.\n- **Veterans’ health care choice**, allowing veterans more access to private/community care outside VA facilities.\n- **Restrictions on abortion funding and some gender-affirming care**, depending on the Republican official or state.\n\nIn short: Republicans usually argue that health care should be **private-sector driven, less regulated, more transparent, and less dependent on federal programs**, while still preserving programs like Medicare for eligible seniors. ([presidency.ucsb.edu](https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/2024-republican-party-platform?utm_source=openai))", "transcript": "What are Republicans' views on health care?\n", "asr_s": 0.61, "expert_s": 7.42, "expert_input_samples": 38620, "expert_input_s": 2.414, "expert_input_sha256": "d57fe5eb396272d1174f540ae6760d1c15e8d49360db9415a0a7d676d89ac24a", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 7.649, "relay_synth_ms": 11769, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0080_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "57be2fdb646464e49f1bdfe49f3ab8fbf523cd2cc1beedc3ec52b2f39808ccca", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 25.04}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0080_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "172c1c705baa9c5fd7a13d6925730c9ac7a4611a3d9aa54e7ae48482e3410e9a", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0080_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "1daf80366d715d64d3ed18fa9d9e983d4a35c716c5292b480a7fce8a02e455d5", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 0.6}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.061, 1.112, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.064, 2.114, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.414, 2.477, 2.527, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.414, 3.477, 3.936, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.414, "last_real_feed_done": 2.477, "onset": 3.936, "gate_read_done": 3.936, "fire": 3.936, "candidate_first_pcm": 3.936, "stall_note": 3.937, "stall_fir