{"id": "swebq0220", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 137555400, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "aa7a8a6f2040793a4fe8dabcb6d10f2520887b0e0988d37809c3a27ef31575d8", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "what makes elvis presley famous?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0220.wav", "input_sha256": "a56770edeae0cb2811f3390e9679b99600538db9178b6bd59385cc16c80b5ed8", "input_samples": 33419, "input_s": 2.089, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.3521, "act": 0.9957, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Elvis Presley is famous for being a pioneering American singer and performer known as the “King of Rock and Roll.” He helped popularize rock and roll in the 1950s with hits like “Heartbreak Hotel,” “Hound Dog,” “Jailhouse Rock,” and “Can’t Help Falling in Love.” His distinctive voice, energetic stage presence, dance moves, and blending of blues, country, and gospel made him one of the most influential musicians of the 20th century.", "expert_answer": "Elvis Presley is famous for being a pioneering American singer and performer known as the **“King of Rock and Roll.”** He helped popularize rock and roll in the 1950s with hits like **“Heartbreak Hotel,” “Hound Dog,” “Jailhouse Rock,”** and **“Can’t Help Falling in Love.”** His distinctive voice, energetic stage presence, dance moves, and blending of blues, country, and gospel made him one of the most influential musicians of the 20th century.", "transcript": "What makes Elvis Presley famous?\n", "asr_s": 0.67, "expert_s": 2.93, "expert_input_samples": 33419, "expert_input_s": 2.089, "expert_input_sha256": "a56770edeae0cb2811f3390e9679b99600538db9178b6bd59385cc16c80b5ed8", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 2.203, "relay_synth_ms": 15475, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_see